1. Setting Up Persistent Volumes (PVs)
The first step in this lab was to create 6 Persistent Volumes (PVs) for the Redis pods. Each Redis pod will need its own dedicated storage for data persistence, which is crucial for stateful applications like Redis.

Step-by-Step:
Create a file called redis-pvs.yaml:
(use nano)
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: redis01
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 1Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  hostPath:
    path: /redis01
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: redis02
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 1Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  hostPath:
    path: /redis02
---
